---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Modelling · Sundharesan Kumaresan"
  description="A modelling portfolio with nothing in it yet. On purpose. The frame stays honest: empty."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-page px-6 pt-16 pb-16">
    <PageHeader left="An aspiration" right="Not yet" title="Modelling" />

    <p data-reveal class="mt-8 max-w-[22ch] font-serif text-statement font-semibold leading-[1.05]">A portfolio page with nothing in it yet. On purpose.</p>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] md:items-center md:gap-16">
      <figure data-reveal class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[340px]">
        <div class="relative flex aspect-[4/5] w-full items-center justify-center border border-border">
          <span class="absolute left-3 top-3 h-2 w-2 bg-stellar"></span>
          <span class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-kicker text-text-muted">No photo yet</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-dateline text-text-muted">Nº 01 · unshot</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div data-reveal class="max-w-[56ch] space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text">
        <p>I've never modelled. No shoots, no catalogue, no agent sending a PDF called “Sundharesan Selects”. There are a few decent shots somewhere, but I have kept them off the internet. Mystery, mostly. Also an entirely reasonable fear of making an Instagram carousel.</p>
        <p>The urge has been hanging around for years now, annoyingly persistent, so it earned its own page. This is me giving it a proper chance to take shape. Maybe it becomes something. Maybe I discover I am not nearly as photogenic before coffee as I had hoped. Either way, when there is work worth showing, it lands here.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
